---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="I'm a dev"
	pubDate={new Date('September 15 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
    Hi, I'm Marcus Wyatt.
  </p>

  <p>
    I'm a software developer with more than 10 years of experience building and maintaining web applications. My primary focus has been Ruby on Rails, but I also work extensively with Docker, AWS, TypeScript, CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, and developer tooling.
  </p>

  <p>
    Throughout my career, I've worked on everything from new feature development to legacy system modernization, production troubleshooting, infrastructure improvements, and team processes. I enjoy solving practical problems, improving developer workflows, and helping teams deliver software more effectively.
  </p>

  <p>
    Some topics you'll frequently find on this blog include:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Ruby on Rails</li>
    <li>RSpec and automated testing</li>
    <li>Docker and development environments</li>
    <li>GitHub Actions and CI/CD</li>
    <li>Developer productivity</li>
    <li>Code review processes</li>
    <li>Software architecture</li>
    <li>Team leadership and engineering practices</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    I believe many of the most valuable lessons in software development come from real-world experience rather than toy examples. The articles here focus on problems I've encountered, solutions I've implemented, mistakes I've made, and ideas that have helped my teams build and maintain software more effectively.
  </p>

  <p>
    When I'm not writing code, I'm usually spending time with my family, exploring new tools and technologies, or working on side projects.
  </p>

  <p>
    If an article helps you solve a problem, teaches you something new, or sparks a different way of thinking about a challenge, then it's done its job.
  </p>

  <p>
    Thanks for reading.
	</p>
</Layout>
